    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d679">

                <pb facs="0806" n="714" xml:id="pg714"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 862.85/522</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chargé in Peru</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Smith</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-08-03T18:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 3, 1918, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s May 29, 3 p.m., June 19, 3 p.m., August 1, 6 p.m.,<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d679-f1"/> your June 3, 9 p.m. Cable Department full report of
                    present status of negotiations for lease from Peru of ex-German ships.</p>
                <p>You are cautioned against saying anything to Peruvian Government regarding
                    guarantee which the United States Government is prepared to make to Peru,
                    against possible consequences which may come from use of German ships. When it
                    becomes necessary again to discuss this guarantee the Department desires to make
                    it a financial one and include it in the actual contract for the ships as was
                    done in the lease for the ex-German ships in Uruguay.</p>
                <p>Before undertaking patrol duty in Peruvian harbors, Navy Department desires
                    specific assurance that arrangement is approved by Peruvian Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
